  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I think a good addition to VRChat would be more options to better adjust the ingame graphics. I dont just mean what part of the avatars show, but to be able to edit the menu to have a different look, changing the current mouse icon from the trail thing to a normal mouse, as so on. I think this would help a bit with both performance and for allowing people to better customize their experience ingame. Another thing I thought of but its less practical, allow menu skins, similar to how Steam or Osu can edit their menu looks, you could create a skin, add it ingame, and the menus look different to you based on how you like it. This will allow not just for skins people like better, but for skins that may add better performance. These ideas probably have been said before, so this may seem repetitive, and im sorry for that, but I do think that this will help the game. Akso to make the loading screen to be a flat static image instead of the 3D one for desktop users, but that ones just a personal one.",
